+### But the SSH comparison has a second flaw: means vs snapshots
+
+Mercator's global attributes say it plainly:
+
+```bash
+python3 -c "
+import xarray as xr
+m = xr.open_dataset('.../MERCATOR_20260717_00.nc')
+for k,v in m.attrs.items(): print('%-12s %s' % (k,v))
+"
+```
+```
+title        daily mean fields from Global Ocean Physics Analysis and Forecast
+```
+
+**Mercator's fields are daily means.** Everything above compared them against CROCO
+*instantaneous* history records. That penalises the finer grid for variability the
+reference has already averaged away — and a 2.5 km grid sub-stepping 3× has a lot more
+high-frequency energy than a 9 km one.
+
+(The variable's own `cell_methods` says only `area: mean`, which is why this is easy to
+miss. The global `title` is the authority.)
+
+Compare like with like. `croco_avg.nc` holds **6-hourly** means (the driver sets
+`NAVG` to 6 h), so average four consecutive records to build the day:
+
+```bash
+D=~/seaforward/forecast/model-runs/Agulhas_AGRIF/20260717_1way/spinup/CROCO_FILES
+cp $D/croco_avg.nc /tmp/ag_pavg.nc; cp $D/croco_avg.nc.1 /tmp/ag_cavg.nc
+
+cd ~/seaforward
+python3 << 'PYEOF'
+import xarray as xr, numpy as np, pandas as pd
+MERC = ('forecast/model-runs/Agulhas_AGRIF/20260717_1way/'
+        'downloaded_data/MERCATOR/MERCATOR_20260717_00.nc')
+m = xr.open_dataset(MERC)
+T0, T1 = 9693.0, 9694.0          # day 2 of the spin-up
+
+def daily(f):
+    d = xr.open_dataset(f, decode_times=False)
+    t = d.scrum_time.values/86400.0
+    k = np.where((t > T0) & (t <= T1))[0]      # the four 6h means inside the day
+    return d, d.zeta.isel(time=k).mean('time').where(d.mask_rho==1).values
+
+p, pz = daily('/tmp/ag_pavg.nc')
+c, cz = daily('/tmp/ag_cavg.nc')
+
+# Mercator daily means are LABELLED AT THE START of their day -> take T0's label,
+# not the window centre. argmin on the centre sits equidistant between two records.
+k = int(np.abs(m.time.values - np.datetime64(
+        pd.Timestamp('2000-01-01') + pd.Timedelta(days=T0))).argmin())
+zos = m.zos.isel(time=k)
+
+def diff(ds, z, mask=None):
+    lo, la = ds.lon_rho.values, ds.lat_rho.values
+    mi = zos.interp(longitude=xr.DataArray(lo,dims=['eta','xi']),
+                    latitude =xr.DataArray(la,dims=['eta','xi'])).values
+    mi = np.where(ds.mask_rho.values==1, mi, np.nan)
+    zz = z.copy()
+    if mask is not None: zz = np.where(mask, zz, np.nan); mi = np.where(mask, mi, np.nan)
+    d = (zz - np.nanmean(zz)) - (mi - np.nanmean(mi))
+    return float(np.sqrt(np.nanmean(d**2)))
+
+lo0,lo1 = float(c.lon_rho.min()), float(c.lon_rho.max())
+la0,la1 = float(c.lat_rho.min()), float(c.lat_rho.max())
+inbox = ((p.lon_rho.values>=lo0)&(p.lon_rho.values<=lo1)&
+         (p.lat_rho.values>=la0)&(p.lat_rho.values<=la1))
+
+print('daily-mean SSH anomaly RMSE (m):')
+print('  parent whole domain    %.4f' % diff(p, pz))
+print('  parent child box only  %.4f   <- fair' % diff(p, pz, inbox))
+print('  child                  %.4f' % diff(c, cz))
+PYEOF
+```
+
+![Agulhas AGRIF daily-mean SSH](img/agulhas_ssh_daily.png)
+
+*Daily-mean SSH anomaly, both grids against Mercator's daily mean for the same day.*
+
+```
+daily-mean SSH anomaly RMSE (m):
+  parent whole domain    0.0527
+  parent child box only  0.0481   <- fair
+  child                  0.0520
+```
+
+Side by side with the snapshot comparison:
+
+| | instantaneous | daily mean |
+|---|---|---|
+| parent (child box) | 0.0514 | 0.0481 |
+| child | **0.0677** | **0.0520** |
+| child penalty | **+32%** | **+8%** |
+
+**Averaging removed three-quarters of the gap.** Most of what looked like the child
+being worse was high-frequency variability the daily-mean reference had already
+smoothed out.
+
+An 8% gap survives — same water, both 24-hour means. Small, and consistent with the
+child resolving shelf structure Mercator cannot represent, but not zero, and this data
+cannot distinguish that from genuine error.
+
